 {
  "index": 4,
  "label": "text",
  "content": "When I carried the first hive up four flights of stairs in a Salisbury removals box, I assumed the hard part was over. It was not. The roof above our flat in Ayr is exposed to every wind the Firth can send, and for the first month the colony hummed in a way that suggested it agreed.",
